cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Skyline fMRI in your research, please cite this software and the
  DIPY and FURY papers it is built on (listed under references).
title: "Skyline fMRI: functional, structural and diffusion MRI visualization built on DIPY Skyline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shah
    given-names: Atharva
repository-code: "https://github.com/Atharva-Shah-2298/skyline-fmri"
url: "https://github.com/Atharva-Shah-2298/skyline-fmri"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
abstract: >-
  Skyline fMRI extends DIPY's Skyline viewer with BOLD time-series playback,
  thresholded activation overlays, task GLM and seed-correlation analyses,
  linking of white-matter tracts to activation clusters, 2D triplanar views
  and high-resolution figure capture, in one GPU-accelerated scene with
  anatomy, diffusion maps and tractography.
keywords:
  - fMRI
  - diffusion MRI
  - tractography
  - visualization
  - neuroimaging
  - DIPY
  - FURY
references:
